================================================================================
CONCLUSION
================================================================================

The centroid-based octree assignment is FUNDAMENTALLY FLAWED for
tetrahedral meshes where elements can span multiple octants.

SOLUTION:
  Assign elements to ALL octree leaves they intersect (bounding-box based),
  not just the leaf containing their centroid.

